[init_plan_agent_1]: {"code_block":"def build_pipeline(train_df, test_df):\n    target_col = \"median_house_value\"\n\n    train_split, valid_split = train_test_split(\n        train_df, test_size=0.2, random_state=42\n    )\n\n    data = skrub.var(\"data\", train_split)\n    X = data.drop(columns=[target_col], errors=\"ignore\").skb.mark_as_X()\n    y = data[target_col].skb.mark_as_y()\n\n    vectorizer = skrub.TableVectorizer()\n    model = CatBoostRegressor(\n        loss_function=\"RMSE\",\n        iterations=1000,\n        depth=8,\n        learning_rate=0.03,\n        eval_metric=\"RMSE\",\n        random_seed=42,\n        verbose=False,\n    )\n\n    learner_plan = X.skb.apply(vectorizer).skb.apply(model, y=y)\n    learner = learner_plan.skb.make_learner(fitted=True)\n\n    X_valid = valid_split.drop(columns=[target_col], errors=\"ignore\")\n    y_valid = valid_split[target_col].values\n    valid_preds = learner.predict({\"data\": X_valid})\n    final_validation_score = mean_squared_error(y_valid, valid_preds) ** 0.5\n    print(f\"Final Validation Performance: {final_validation_score}\")\n\n    full_data = skrub.var(\"data\", train_df)\n    X_full = full_data.drop(columns=[target_col], errors=\"ignore\").skb.mark_as_X()\n    y_full = full_data[target_col].skb.mark_as_y()\n    full_plan = X_full.skb.apply(vectorizer).skb.apply(model, y=y_full)\n    full_learner = full_plan.skb.make_learner(fitted=True)\n\n    test_preds = full_learner.predict({\"data\": test_df})\n    return test_preds","plan":"Keep the DataOps graph intact, but focus improvement on CatBoost rather than TableVectorizer since the ablation showed the vectorizer had no measurable effect while CatBoost settings dominated RMSE. The next step is a small, localized tuning pass over a few impactful CatBoost parameters (for example depth, learning rate, l2_leaf_reg, subsample, and iterations) using a bounded search budget, rather than expanding preprocessing. If tuning is used in the final pass, materi